Ladybird lays a background image of an inline box broken across lines
out over one strip as long as all of the box’s pieces, and each piece
paints its own slice of it. Blink does the same, in its
InlineBoxFragmentPainterBase::PaintRectForImageStrip(), which offsets
each fragment by the width of the fragments before it. WebKit does in
InlineBoxPainter::paintFillLayer(). And Gecko’s InlineBackgroundData::
GetContinuousRect() gives each continuation the joined rect of all of
them. Ladybird doesn’t implement “box-decoration-break: clone” yet,
so pieces keep their own backgrounds under it, as before.
